```text
1. Add WebFrontendServiceImpl as a new FrontendService adapter for the web mode
    [x] 'content/modules/web_frontend/__init__.py': New subpackage init, exports the impl
        - `from .web_frontend_service import *`
    [x] 'content/modules/web_frontend/web_frontend_service.py': Self-contained web frontend service + internal HTTP handler
        - `_ReplySlot`: tiny threading helper — holds an `Event` + `bytes` payload; `.wait()` blocks, `.resolve(payload)` fires
        - `_Handler(http.server.SimpleHTTPRequestHandler)`: serves static files from `web-ui/frontend/` dir; proxies `/v1/chat/completions`, `/api/desktop-mode`, `/api/inference-mode` to `self.server.gpu_box_url`; on `GET /api/prompt` builds two `KbCmd`s (`'q'` then `'a'`), creates a `_ReplySlot`, stashes it in `self.server.frontend._pending` keyed by `id(cmd)`, pushes both cmds onto `self.server.frontend._queue`, blocks on `.wait()`, writes the bytes back as `text/plain`
        - `WebFrontendServiceImpl(FrontendService)`: `__init__` takes `port`, `gpu_box_url`; creates the `Queue`, pre-puts `BootCmd()`, creates `dict[int, _ReplySlot]` for `_pending`, builds the `HTTPServer`, attaches `self` and `gpu_box_url` onto the server instance, spawns a daemon `threading.Thread` targeting `serve_forever`
        - `__post_init__`: starts the daemon thread
        - `get_request`: `return self._queue.get()`
        - `post_response`: match on result type — `StartResult` → print ready; `ExitResult` → no-op; anything else → `slot = self._pending.pop(id(result.cmd), None)`; if slot exists, `slot.resolve(result.text.encode("utf-8"))`; if not, no-op (handles the intermediate domain-select result with no attached slot)
        - static file dir computed from `Path(__file__)` → `content/web-ui/frontend`
        - prohibition: do NOT import or subclass the existing `WebServer` or `ProxyHandler` from `web_clanker.py`; this is fully independent
    [x] 'content/modules/__init__.py': Add one import line for the new subpackage
        - `from .web_frontend.web_frontend_service import WebFrontendServiceImpl`
    [x] 'content/clanker.py': Add `newserver` subcommand and wiring block
        - add `sub.add_parser("newserver", help="Start the web frontend (new)")`
        - new `if args.mode == "newserver":` branch: construct `WebFrontendServiceImpl(port=8787, gpu_box_url="https://gpu-box.tailca68f1.ts.net:8787")`, then the same `files_adapter`, `cfg_ingestor`, `ingestion`, `prompt_service`, `kb_service` as the other paths, build `AppEngine(frontend=frontend, ...)`, call `engine.run()`
        - prohibition: do NOT modify or remove the existing `server` subcommand or its wiring; it stays as-is
```

