2. Add GET /api/char?char=X endpoint to _Handler for single-char commands
    [x] 'content/modules/web_frontend/web_frontend_service.py': Add char endpoint to _Handler.do_GET + fix post_response for non-text results
        - in `do_GET`: add branch `elif self.path.startswith("/api/char"):` before the generic `/api/` 404
        - parse query via `urllib.parse.urlsplit(self.path).query` → `urllib.parse.parse_qs` → extract `char` key (single non-empty string)
        - if missing/invalid: `400` with `text/plain` body `"Missing or invalid 'char' query param"`
        - build `cmd = KbCmd(char=char_val)`, create `slot = _ReplySlot()`, stash `frontend._pending[id(cmd)] = slot`
        - push `frontend._queue.put(cmd)`, block on `body = slot.wait()`
        - write back as `200` / `text/plain` with `Content-Length`
        - add `from urllib.parse import parse_qs, urlsplit` at top of file
        - in `post_response` catch-all `case _:`: guard with `hasattr(result, "text")` before `slot.resolve(...)`
        - if no `.text` (DomainSelectedResult, UnboundKeyResult, etc.): resolve with `repr(type(result).__name__).encode("utf-8")` so the slot unblocks and the handler returns a status string instead of crashing
